INT. COLLAPSED COPPER MINE, CHAMBER 7 - NIGHT

A pocket of dark rock, the ceiling low enough to touch. A single lantern burns blue on the last of the oil. Dust floats in the beam like drifting ash. Somewhere beyond the rubble, water drips.

Three miners sit against the walls. AGNIESZKA PETROVA-LUU (40s, helmet cracked, hands bloodied) tends the lantern. OLUSEGUN HARTMANN-BELL (30s, wiry, one arm in a makeshift sling) stares at the cave-in. DOMINGO REYES-ASANTE (60s, gray-faced, a tin lunch pail on his lap) hums an old hymn.

AGNIESZKA
Three days, Segun.

OLUSEGUN
Two and a half.

AGNIESZKA
We've counted the same.

OLUSEGUN
Then we've counted wrong.

DOMINGO
Hush, both of you. The air.

AGNIESZKA
What about the air?

DOMINGO
It's thin. Talk less. Think slower.

OLUSEGUN
I can't think slower.

DOMINGO
Then pray.

OLUSEGUN
To what? To Chamber Seven?

DOMINGO
Pray to whoever is listening.

Silence. The lantern sputters. Agnieszka reaches for the oil can, shakes it. A thin trickle.

AGNIESZKA
That's the last.

OLUSEGUN
Then we're done.

AGNIESZKA
We're not done.

OLUSEGUN
Agnieszka, we are in a hole.

AGNIESZKA
We are in a hole with a lunch pail, a lantern, and an old man who knows every tunnel in this mountain.

DOMINGO
(chuckles)
Every tunnel but this one.

AGNIESZKA
Because it doesn't exist.

DOMINGO
Because nobody lived to draw it.

A long pause. Olusegun lowers his head to his knees. Domingo opens the pail. Inside, a single boiled egg wrapped in cloth. He splits it carefully into three pieces.

DOMINGO (CONT'D)
My wife packed it. She always packs two. I forgot the other this morning.

He passes the pieces. They eat, slowly, as if tasting something holy.

A faint scrape comes from the rubble. They freeze. Another scrape, then a tap, tap, tap, tap.

OLUSEGUN
Rats.

AGNIESZKA
Too regular.

DOMINGO
Quiet.

They scramble toward the wall of stone. Agnieszka presses her ear to it. Olusegun scrabbles at a loose rock. Domingo lifts the lantern.

A stone shifts. A headlamp stabs through a fist-sized gap, then a hand, then a grimy face: RESCUER JOSIAH WELLINGTON-OKORO (30s, orange helmet, dust-black cheeks), wriggling in on his belly.

RESCUER
Hello? Is anyone alive in here?

Olusegun sobs. Agnieszka laughs. Domingo closes his eyes and finishes his hymn.
